{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789423807,"nonce":"hntEw+MYPzIcHqLPS2Ll2MD+E58=","message":"The loop-header poll landed as a polling page (HotSpot's shape):\nevery compiled loop header loads a word from a page; World::stop\nmprotects it PROT_NONE, the load faults, and the SIGSEGV/SIGBUS\nhandler parks the thread with its stack pointer and registers taken\nfrom the ucontext (the registers go into a thread-local buffer the\ncollector scans as an extra range). Each program maps its own page\n(baked into its JIT code via a per-compile thread-local, carried on\nthe engine), so isolates in one process do not stall each other;\nAOT code references the static wlift_safepoint_page by symbol, which\na stop protects too. The first shape was a flag load + compare +\nbranch: +10% on nbody and +7% on mandelbrot on the NUC; the page\nload costs +2% on nbody and nothing on mandelbrot, the rest\nunchanged. A process-global page was tried first and livelocked the\nstressed e2e suite: single-threaded VMs in the same process faulted\non other tests' stops forever.\n\nA compiled spin loop on a worker now answers a collection driven by\nthe main thread (e2e compiled_loop_answers_a_collector_on_another_\nthread; the same script hangs on the commit before). Suites, corpus\n(tiered and AOT), site pass; AOT thread tests run.\n\nStages 1–4 are in. Left: a Thread handle from create; List/Map\nraces are the program's (Go's rule); hatch-web's loop onto the\nruntime scheduler is hatch's call; 09e7faa is the older abort-path\nflake the hot+stress corpus shows.","files":null}]}